          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mrwoi0251smz1yj8",
          "message": {
            "text": "**Why an env marker** (`HOTSHEET_DRIVE_SPAWNED=1`) rather than detecting the parent process: the channel server is spawned by the *agent* (codex/agy/opencode), not by Hot Sheet directly, so there is no direct parent-pid relationship to inspect — but env propagates transitively from the drive spawn (`codexDrive.ts:115`, `antigravityDrive.ts`, `acp/acpDrive.ts:105`) through the agent to its MCP children. Mirrors the HS-9038 `worktree` marker one field up. See also `src/channelRegistry.ts` (`mainConnections`).\n",
            "markdown": "**Why an env marker** (`HOTSHEET_DRIVE_SPAWNED=1`) rather than detecting the parent process: the channel server is spawned by the *agent* (codex/agy/opencode), not by Hot Sheet directly, so there is no direct parent-pid relationship to inspect — but env propagates transitively from the drive spawn (`codexDrive.ts:115`, `antigravityDrive.ts`, `acp/acpDrive.ts:105`) through the agent to its MCP children. Mirrors the HS-9038 `worktree` marker one field up. See also `src/channelRegistry.ts` (`mainConnections`).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/channel.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 527,
                  "endLine": 536,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      // not as duplicate main connections. (Light readFileSettings check, not the\n      // heavier `worktrees.ts::isFollowerWorktree`, to keep the channel bundle lean.)\n      worktree: isFollowerCwd() ? process.cwd() : null,\n      // HS-9380 — tag this connection as a play/command DRIVE's when the agent that\n      // spawned us was itself spawned by a Hot Sheet drive (`codex exec` /\n      // `agy --print` / an ACP session). The drives export `HOTSHEET_DRIVE_SPAWNED=1`\n      // into the agent's env, which propagates to its MCP children (us). Lets the\n      // multi-connection warning + leader pick + cleanup treat these expected,\n      // temporary connections like worker connections rather than duplicate mains.\n      drive: process.env.HOTSHEET_DRIVE_SPAWNED === '1' ? true : null,"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
